  "finalText": "The ligand in PDB entry 1HSG is **MK1**, which is the HIV protease inhibitor indinavir. I looked this up with the RCSB PDB GraphQL tools on rightclick-x.\n\n- **What's bound:** non-polymer entity 2 of 1HSG is a single molecule of component MK1, sitting in chain B (label_asym C). Its full name is N-[2(R)-hydroxy-1(S)-indanyl]-5-[(2(S)-tertiary butylaminocarbonyl)-4(3-pyridylmethyl)piperazino]-4(S)-hydroxy-2(R)-phenylmethylpentanamide. Looking up entity 3 as a non-polymer returned nothing, so MK1 is the only non-water small molecule I found.\n- **Chemical component dictionary entry for MK1:**\n  - Formula: C36 H47 N5 O4\n  - Formula weight: 613.789 g/mol\n  - The dictionary links this component to indinavir (ATC code J05AE02, matched by InChIKey in DrugBank).\n\nThe entity record lists the formula weight as 0.614 because it's given in kDa. It's the same value.\n\nANSWER: MK1 | C36 H47 N5 O4 | 613.789"
